l","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{W}","name":"Samite Healer","oracle_id":"95a0ca48-d924-47f4-86ed-42c673ee778c","oracle_text":"{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-07-13","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Human Cleric"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":["Equip"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Viridian Longbow","oracle_id":"8b9119b0-9948-497f-aa92-2879d07bed1c","oracle_text":"Equipped creature has \"{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target.\"\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2021-07-23","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact — Equipment"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Split second"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{R}{R}","name":"Word of Seizing","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","oracle_text":"Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\nUntap target permanent and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"You only gain the life when the triggered ability resolves. If you are reduced to zero life before the ability resolves, you will lose before gaining the life.","oracle_id":"1f35f5e3-ddd1-4293-96f8-1181bbda77eb","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"1f35f5e3-ddd1-4293-96f8-1181bbda77eb","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"1f35f5e3-ddd1-4293-96f8-1181bbda77eb","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn't provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"34b4d137-780b-446c-8cdd-fd1673180971","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it's no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"34b4d137-780b-446c-8cdd-fd1673180971","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Slivercycling is a form of cycling. Any ability that triggers on a card being cycled also triggers on Slivercycling a card. Any ability that stops a cycling ability from being activated also stops Slivercycling from being activated.","oracle_id":"34b4d137-780b-446c-8cdd-fd1673180971","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Unlike a normal cycling ability, Slivercycling doesn't have you draw a card. Instead, it lets you search your library for a Sliver card.","oracle_id":"34b4d137-780b-446c-8cdd-fd1673180971","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card’s controller controls the triggered ability, but the controller of the Sliver that deals damage to a player decides whether or not to put the token onto the battlefield under their control.","oracle_id":"6b1d178f-9713-4dcf-920b-ddf2c94cc427","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"6b1d178f-9713-4dcf-920b-ddf2c94cc427","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"6b1d178f-9713-4dcf-920b-ddf2c94cc427","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
